---
kind: scene
id: south.moonstoneDig
title: The dig under Moonstone Cave
on: enterPlace
target: place.moonstoneCave
once: false
after: 'visited("south.moonstoneCave")'
when: "run.lair.quarryDig != 'cleared' && @southDigOpen"
---

// CONTRACT BEAT (seeded by the lead; owned by south): moves run.lair.quarryDig
// hidden -> found -> cleared and asserts defeated(gruntDig). The first
// entry (south.moonstoneCave) finds the dig; this beat, once the three ramp
// grunts are down, fights the Digmaster, clears it, and lets the player
// carry one fossil out (run.southFossil) for the Pebbleton museum.

## The pit

::bg{location="moonstone-dig" time="night"}
::music{playback="change" mood="tense" volume="normal"}
::set{run.lair.quarryDig = "found" when="run.lair.quarryDig == 'hidden'"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: The cart tracks end at a pit lit like a stage. Fossils lie in rows on tarpaulins, each one labelled in a neat hand: SPIRAL. DOME. DOME. SPIRAL.
@gruntDig{code="0010"}: You got past my ramp crew? Three of them? I'll be writing a report about that.
::use{component="trainerBattle" who="gruntDig" intro="Eclipse is digging here! These fossils belong to the Director. Scram, kid!" win="Urgh! The Director won't like this." lose="Heh. Stay out of Eclipse business." prize="600" instance="use-001"}
::set{run.lair.quarryDig = "cleared" when="@wonFight"}

## After the fight

<match subject="scene.battle.fight.won">
  <when is="true">
    @gruntDig{code="0020"}: Fine. Keep the rocks. The Director already has the one that matters, and it isn't in this hole.
    ::music{playback="change" mood="calm" volume="down"}
    @narrator{code="0020"}: The grunts pack up their lights and run. The fossil pit is quiet. The dig is {{run.lair.quarryDig}}.
    @narrator{code="0030"}: Most of the tarpaulins went with them. Two fossils are left in the mud: a smooth dome of shell, and a spiral like a stone snail.
    <branch id="southDigFossil" prompt="You can carry one of them out.">
      <choice id="dome" text="The dome fossil" into="run.southFossil" value="dome">
        @narrator{code="0040"}: The dome is heavier than it looks. Something inside it seems to shift when you lift it.
      </choice>
      <choice id="spiral" text="The spiral fossil" into="run.southFossil" value="spiral">
        @narrator{code="0050"}: The spiral fits in your two hands exactly, as if it had been waiting for them.
      </choice>
    </branch>
    @narrator{code="0060"}: The museum in Pebbleton would know what to do with a fossil like this.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator{code="0070"}: The work lights come back on, one by one. The picks start again as if you had never been there.
  </otherwise>
</match>
